IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- s 216B, "Evidence of shareholders' approval not decisive -- Court approval to discontinue action under section 216A"
-- (LAYER 1: the law, objectively; part sgf).
--
-- What is here: the bar on staying or dismissing an application or action by reason only of the members' approval, and the Court's
-- power to take that evidence into account (s 216B(1)); the bar on a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of
-- prosecution without the Court's approval, the Court's power to give approval on terms and to order notice to the complainant
-- (s 216B(2)); the Court's power to order interim costs and the complainant's liability to account for them (s 216B(3)).
--
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE the text says yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not say.
-- Every provision here is about "an application made or an action brought or intervened in under section 216A": that is the scope
-- gate, asked as a fact. Outside it the text says nothing (a scope limit with no "only": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)).

§ `Section 216B(1): the members' approval is not decisive`

-- (1), first limb: "An application made or an action brought or intervened in under section 216A must not be stayed or dismissed by
-- reason only that it is shown that an alleged breach of a right or duty owed to the company has been or may be approved by the
-- members of the company". A flat negative named as the bar. Where the stay or dismissal rests on something else too, or the
-- proceeding is not one under s 216A, the case is outside the limit the bar sets for itself ("by reason only"; "under section 216A"):
-- NOTHING (fork F-216B-1). There is no case in which the text says the bar does not apply.
-- src:21862 | 216B.—(1) An application made or an action brought or intervened
-- src:21863 | in under section 216A must not be stayed or dismissed by reason only
-- src:21864 | that it is shown that an alleged breach of a right or duty owed to the
-- src:21865 | company has been or may be approved by the members of the
-- src:21866 | company, but evidence of approval by the members may be taken into
@ref s 216B(1) (src:21862-21866)
GIVEN `the application is made, or the action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason for the stay or dismissal is that it is shown that an alleged breach of a right or duty owed to the company has been or may be approved by the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216B(1) the stay or dismissal is barred where the only reason is the members' approval of the alleged breach` MEANS
    IF    `the application is made, or the action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A`
      AND `the only reason for the stay or dismissal is that it is shown that an alleged breach of a right or duty owed to the company has been or may be approved by the members of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not be stayed or dismissed by reason only that it is shown that an alleged breach ... has been or may be approved by the members" -- a prohibition limited by "by reason only" and by "under section 216A"; a stay or dismissal for another reason, or of another proceeding, is outside the limit

-- (1), second limb: "but evidence of approval by the members may be taken into account by the Court in making an order under
-- section 216A". A power ("may be taken into account"), limited to evidence of approval by the members and to the making of an order
-- under s 216A: outside them the answer is NOTHING (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-216B-2).
-- src:21866 | company, but evidence of approval by the members may be taken into
-- src:21867 | account by the Court in making an order under section 216A.
@ref s 216B(1) (src:21866-21867)
GIVEN `there is evidence of approval by the members of the alleged breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is making an order under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216B(1) the Court may take evidence of approval by the members into account in making an order under section 216A` MEANS
    IF `there is evidence of approval by the members of the alleged breach` AND `the Court is making an order under section 216A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence of approval by the members may be taken into account by the Court in making an order under section 216A" -- a grant limited to that evidence and that making of an order; the text does not say the Court may not take other matters into account

§ `Section 216B(2): the Court's approval to stay, discontinue, settle or dismiss`

-- What is sought of the application or action.
DECLARE `s 216B(2) what is sought` IS ONE OF
    `s 216B(2) a stay`
    `s 216B(2) a discontinuance`
    `s 216B(2) a settlement`
    `s 216B(2) a dismissal for want of prosecution`
    `s 216B(2) a dismissal for another reason`

-- (2), first limb: "must not be stayed, discontinued, settled or dismissed for want of prosecution without the approval of the Court
-- given upon such terms as the Court thinks fit". A flat negative named as the bar. "For want of prosecution" is read as qualifying
-- only "dismissed" (fork F-216B-3): a dismissal for another reason is not in the list and the text does not say. With the Court's
-- approval ("without") the case is outside the limit the bar sets for itself: NOTHING (fork F-216B-4).
-- src:21872 | (2) An application made or an action brought or intervened in under
-- src:21873 | section 216A must not be stayed, discontinued, settled or dismissed
-- src:21874 | for want of prosecution without the approval of the Court given upon
-- src:21875 | such terms as the Court thinks fit and, if the Court determines that the
@ref s 216B(2) (src:21872-21875)
GIVEN `the application is made, or the action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN
      sought IS A `s 216B(2) what is sought`
      `the Court has approved it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216B(2) the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution is barred without the approval of the Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the application is made, or the action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application made or an action brought or intervened in under section 216A must not be stayed" -- a scope limit with no "only"; another proceeding is outside it
        IF sought EQUALS `s 216B(2) a dismissal for another reason`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "stayed, discontinued, settled or dismissed for want of prosecution" lists four things without "only"; a dismissal for another reason is not one of them, and the text does not say it is permitted
        IF `the Court has approved it`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not be stayed ... without the approval of the Court" -- with the approval the case is outside the limit the prohibition sets for itself
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2), first limb, the Court's side: "the approval of the Court given upon such terms as the Court thinks fit". A power to attach
-- terms to its approval; limited to approval of the things the subsection lists in a proceeding under s 216A (grant ruling of
-- 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-216B-7).
-- src:21872 | (2) An application made or an action brought or intervened in under
-- src:21873 | section 216A must not be stayed, discontinued, settled or dismissed
-- src:21874 | for want of prosecution without the approval of the Court given upon
-- src:21875 | such terms as the Court thinks fit and, if the Court determines that the
@ref s 216B(2) (src:21872-21875)
GIVEN `the application is made, or the action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is giving its approval to the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216B(2) the Court may give its approval upon such terms as it thinks fit` MEANS
    IF    `the application is made, or the action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A`
      AND `the Court is giving its approval to the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the approval of the Court given upon such terms as the Court thinks fit" -- a grant tied to approval of a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal in a proceeding under section 216A; elsewhere the text does not say

-- (2), second limb: "if the Court determines that the interest of any complainant may be substantially affected by such stay,
-- discontinuance, settlement or dismissal, the Court may order any party to the application or action to give notice to the
-- complainant". A power whose "if" gate is the Court's own determination (an input): where it fails, NOTHING (grant ruling,
-- limit 1; fork F-216B-5).
