      `the Court has determined that the interest of a complainant may be substantially affected by the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216B(2) the Court may order a party to give notice to the complainant` MEANS
    IF    `the application is made, or the action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A`
      AND `the Court has determined that the interest of a complainant may be substantially affected by the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Court determines that the interest of any complainant may be substantially affected ..., the Court may order any party to the application or action to give notice to the complainant" -- a grant whose "if" gate is not met; the text does not say the Court may not

§ `Section 216B(3): interim costs`

-- (3), first limb: "In an application made or an action brought or intervened in under section 216A, the Court may at any time order the
-- company to pay to the complainant interim costs, including legal fees and disbursements". A power with a scope limit ("In an
-- application ... under section 216A") and no time limit ("at any time"); outside the scope the answer is NOTHING (grant ruling of
-- 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-216B-8).
-- src:21880 | (3) In an application made or an action brought or intervened in
-- src:21881 | under section 216A, the Court may at any time order the company to
-- src:21882 | pay to the complainant interim costs, including legal fees and
@ref s 216B(3) (src:21880-21882)
GIVEN `the application is made, or the action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216B(3) the Court may order the company to pay the complainant interim costs` MEANS
    IF `the application is made, or the action is brought or intervened in, under section 216A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In an application made or an action brought or intervened in under section 216A, the Court may at any time order the company to pay to the complainant interim costs" -- a scope limit with no "only"; another proceeding is outside it

-- (3), "including legal fees and disbursements": the costs the Court may order include these. An "includes" list: a listed item holds,
-- anything else is not covered.
-- src:21881 | under section 216A, the Court may at any time order the company to
-- src:21882 | pay to the complainant interim costs, including legal fees and
@ref s 216B(3) (src:21881-21882)
GIVEN `the costs are legal fees or disbursements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216B(3) the interim costs the Court may order include the item` MEANS
    IF `the costs are legal fees or disbursements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "interim costs, including legal fees and disbursements" does not close the list

-- (3), second limb: "but the complainant may be accountable for such interim costs upon final disposition of the application or
-- action". A "may" gated by "upon": SPLIT SITE (ii). Ruling (c) of the delegated-definitions ruling of 2026-11-05 ("when", "upon" and
-- "whenever" count as "where" under rule (b) of the periods ruling) is taken as the Guide gives it: until final disposition the answer
-- is JUST FALSE. The "In short" line on grants points to NOTHING: fork F-216B-6.
-- src:21882 | pay to the complainant interim costs, including legal fees and
-- src:21883 | disbursements, but the complainant may be accountable for such
-- src:21884 | interim costs upon final disposition of the application or action.
@ref s 216B(3) (src:21882-21884)
GIVEN `the Court has ordered the company to pay the complainant interim costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application or action has been finally disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216B(3) the complainant may be accountable for the interim costs` MEANS
    IF `the Court has ordered the company to pay the complainant interim costs` AND `the application or action has been finally disposed of`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the complainant may be accountable for such interim costs upon final disposition of the application or action" -- a "may" gated by "upon", not met (split site (ii): the delegated-definitions ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); the other reading is NOTHING, fork F-216B-6)
